  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the expression as a square:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}}={(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}})}^{2}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$",
